  "term": "AIDS dementia complex",
  "definition": "AIDS dementia complex is a neurologic disorder linked to AIDS in which HIV-1 affects the central nervous system, leading to problems such as poor concentration and memory, slowed hand movements, unsteady coordination, apathy, incontinence, and difficulty walking.",
